      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: does the threat model actually prevent anything?\nCan we briefly explain the threat model, or link to an explanation?\n\nThe wording seems slightly contorted - rather than \"a threat model considering the host as non-trusted (as used by AVF) should also prevent pVMs from trusting that the virtual platform they are running on has been properly set up\" can we just say something like pVMs must not trust the host, including not to set the VM up properly.",
