        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T17:35:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I get what you mean but it\u0027s transitive: pvmfw addresses the concerns of validating the guest image(s) and provisioning actually-secret secrets thanks to the hypervisor guaranteeing that pvmfw is untampered \u0026 the first thing to run.\n\nThe point of this paragraph is to address _why_ pvmfw is part of AVF and I thought that the following sentence explained its dependency on the hypervisor; what do you suggest I change here?",
      "parentUuid": "d84b9e6c_1c6cfac8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "dfcab85b4a0383ebf87c98909ee73cbec781e040",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad634d23_e8196e59",
        "filename": "pvmfw/README.md",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T12:27:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I think my confusion comes from having the description in a different order to the flow. And the guarantee that we\u0027re running the correct pvmfw is necessary for pvmfw to be able to do its job. It\u0027s partly a passive/active thing - \"by being the very first code\" is begging the question of who is doing that.\n\nSo I would say something along the lines of \"To address these concerns the hypervisor \u003csecurely loads pvmfw and starts it\u003e and then pvmfw \u003cdoes useful \u0026 important stuff\u003e.\"\n\nBut this is all stylistic, feel free to ignore.",
      "parentUuid": "21019603_bd668159",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "dfcab85b4a0383ebf87c98909ee73cbec781e040",
